spec.text:
{
 "id": "T-304",
 "milestone": "M2",
 "depends_on": [
  "T-303"
 ],
 "title": "A round whose only fault is its report keeps its work: the report is fixed without redoing the code, and the class-list check reads a found-and-fixed line with detail in it",
 "public_title": "A refused report no longer throws away the round's work",
 "door": {
  "kind": "one-way",
  "reason": "It changes the plan check in bin/lib/fm_plan.py, which is on the sensitive list."
 },
 "scope": [
  "bin/fm-worker.sh",
  "bin/lib/fm_plan.py",
  "bin/lib/fm_evidence.py",
  "bin/lib/**",
  "skills/worker/**",
  "skills/firstmate/**",
  "tests/**",
  "design/design.md"
 ],
 "acceptance": [
  "Why. Since T-302 a fix round must list the places it checked for the same cause (a SWEPT block with 'found N, fixed M'). When only that report is wrong, the launcher refuses the whole round and pushes nothing. On 2026-10-13 T-303 lost a 49-minute build round because one line read 'found 2 (detail), fixed 2'; T-289 lost three rounds the same way on 2026-10-12. The code was right each time; only the report text was refused.",
  "What, lenient class line. The class-list check accepts detail between and after the numbers, for example 'found 2 (the merge card), fixed 2' or 'found 1, fixed 1 (tests/lib.sh)'. A block still needs a searched line and both numbers; a block with no numbers, or with fixed greater than found, is still refused.",
  "What, report-only refusal keeps the work. When a round is refused only because its report breaks a report rule (class list, plan rows, markers), the round's changes are kept in the worktree, nothing is pushed, and the next round is a report-only round: the worker gets the refusal reason and its own report, fixes the report, and changes no code. The launcher then publishes the kept changes with the fixed report.",
  "What, never wipe kept work. A launch that finds uncommitted work from a refused round of the same pin keeps it in place, whether or not the task already has a pull request; the copy in state/rescued stays as a backup.",
  "What, unchanged. A round refused for its code (scope, tests, gates) is handled as today. External projects keep today's path.",
  "Done, tests. A block with detail between the numbers passes and a block without numbers is still refused (`plan: class line with detail`, fail-first); a report-only refusal keeps the worktree changes and the next round is report-only (`worker: report-only refusal keeps work`, fail-first); a launch on a task with an open pull request keeps a refused round's work in place (`worker: kept work survives a launch with a PR`, fail-first).",
  "Docs. The worker skill and design.md's worker-round section say this in a few lines."
 ],
 "explain": {
  "en": {
   "intent": [
    {
     "kind": "fact",
     "text": "A found-and-fixed line with detail in it passes the check."
    },
    {
     "kind": "fact",
     "text": "A round refused only for its report keeps its code and fixes only the report."
    },
    {
     "kind": "fact",
     "text": "A launch never wipes the kept work of a refused round."
    }
   ],
   "why": [
    {
     "kind": "fact",
     "text": "T-303 lost a 49-minute round over one report line."
    }
   ],
   "scope_in": [
    "the class-list check",
    "the worker launcher",
    "tests"
   ],
   "scope_out": [
    "code refusals",
    "external projects"
   ],
   "done": [
    {
     "kind": "fact",
     "text": "Intent 1: a test shows a line with detail passes."
    },
    {
     "kind": "fact",
     "text": "Intent 2: a test shows a report-only refusal keeps the code."
    },
    {
     "kind": "fact",
     "text": "Intent 3: a test shows the work survives a launch with a pull request."
    }
   ],
   "notes": [
    {
     "kind": "note",
     "text": "A wrong report costs a short round, not a full one."
    }
   ],
   "before_nodes": [
    {
     "state": "same",
     "label": "Round builds"
    },
    {
     "state": "gone",
     "label": "Report refused, work lost"
    },
    {
     "state": "same",
     "label": "Push"
    }
   ],
   "after_nodes": [
    {
     "state": "same",
     "label": "Round builds"
    },
    {
     "state": "new",
     "label": "Fix report only"
    },
    {
     "state": "same",
     "label": "Push"
    }
   ]
  },
  "zh-TW": {
   "intent": [
    {
     "kind": "fact",
     "text": "found 和 fixed 之間有說明文字，檢查照樣通過。"
    },
    {
     "kind": "fact",
     "text": "只有報告不合格時，程式碼保留，只修報告。"
    },
    {
     "kind": "fact",
     "text": "重新啟動不會清掉這些保留的改動。"
    }
   ],
   "why": [
    {
     "kind": "fact",
     "text": "T-303 因為一行報告格式丟掉 49 分鐘的實作。"
    }
   ],
   "scope_in": [
    "同類清單檢查",
    "worker 啟動器",
    "測試"
   ],
   "scope_out": [
    "程式碼本身的拒收",
    "外部專案"
   ],
   "done": [
    {
     "kind": "fact",
     "text": "意圖 1：測試證明帶說明的那一行能通過。"
    },
    {
     "kind": "fact",
     "text": "意圖 2：測試證明只拒收報告時程式碼保留。"
    },
    {
     "kind": "fact",
     "text": "意圖 3：測試證明有 PR 時改動也不會清掉。"
    }
   ],
   "notes": [
    {
     "kind": "note",
     "text": "報告寫錯只多一輪短的修正，不再重做整輪。"
    }
   ],
   "before_nodes": [
    {
     "state": "same",
     "label": "實作"
    },
    {
     "state": "gone",
     "label": "報告拒收，成果丟失"
    },
    {
     "state": "same",
     "label": "推送"
    }
   ],
   "after_nodes": [
    {
     "state": "same",
     "label": "實作"
    },
    {
     "state": "new",
     "label": "只修報告"
    },
    {
     "state": "same",
     "label": "推送"
    }
   ]
  }
 }
}
